{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For the dumbed</b> — like \"on account of.\"" "<b>Prophecy</b> — a noun, from כליל יחלוף יגזור, and likewise the interpretation is: the words of King Lemuel — they are words of burden and prophecy; his mother instructed him." "<b>Sons of passing</b> — sons of death, on account of the judgment of death, and he says they shall investigate it thoroughly."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "Reading the lemma as חלוף (cf. Proverbs 31:1, where the word is traditionally read as מַשָּׂא); the verse reference is implicit.", 2 "The lemma בני חלוף is not the received text of Prov 31:8; possibly Ibn Ezra's text or an interpretive gloss on עֹבְרִים in that verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:51.347562170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}